# Demo content under src/features/project/demoContent/ is bundled and parsed
# verbatim via import.meta.glob(..., { query: '?raw' }). The frontmatter parser
# normalizes line endings, but the bundled fixtures must still never ship CRLF on
# a Windows (core.autocrlf) checkout. Pinning Markdown to LF keeps the committed
# fixtures byte-stable across platforms (defense-in-depth, not the parser fix).
*.md text eol=lf

# TypeScript sources: declare text + LF so line endings stay consistent
# cross-platform and tooling treats them as text. This does not by itself stop a
# stray NUL byte from flipping a file to git-binary (the source must stay
# NUL-free); it is defense-in-depth alongside keeping sources clean.
*.ts text eol=lf
*.tsx text eol=lf
